\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Lemma}
\title{Separated edges add}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Let the edge weights be strictly positive and let #{K} be a
nonempty set of vertices. Suppose the edges are partitioned
into families #{E_i}. Let #{U_i} be the set of vertices
outside #{K} that are incident to #{E_i}, and suppose the sets
#{U_i} are pairwise disjoint. Suppose every edge of #{E_i}
has both ends in #{K\cup U_i}, and every vertex of #{U_i} is
joined to #{K} by a path in #{E_i}. Let #{L_i} be the
Laplacian of the edges #{E_i}. Then #{L_w=\sum_i L_i}. Let
#{h} be the counting inner product, and let the energy of a
function #{x} be #{h(x,(-L_w)x)}. Let #{Z} be the set of
vertices outside #{K} and outside every #{U_i}. No edge meets
#{Z}, so each vertex of #{Z} is isolated and the energy does
not depend on its value. These local assumptions do not
require the graph to be connected, and the minimum below is
not the connected-graph \vocabk{kept form}{fdip-00DF}.}

\p{For a function #{u} on #{K} and for each family, the minimum
of the #{L_i}-energy over extensions of #{u} to #{K\cup U_i}
exists. If #{U_i} is empty, that contribution is the energy
#{h(u,(-L_i)u)} on #{K}. If #{U_i} is nonempty, let #{\iota_{U_i}}
be the inclusion of functions supported on #{U_i}. The
compression #{\iota_{U_i}^{\dagger}(-L_i)\iota_{U_i}} is positive definite, and
the minimizer on #{U_i} is unique. The minimum of
#{h(x,(-L_w)x)} over extensions of #{u} to the whole vertex set
is attained and equals the sum of these local minima. The
minimizer is unique on the active vertices
#{K\cup\bigcup_i U_i} and arbitrary on #{Z}. Global uniqueness
is not claimed, and no vertex is deleted.}

\proof{
\p{Each edge belongs to one family, so the energies add for
every function. A function on #{U_i} does not appear in any
other summand, and a value on #{Z} appears in none. For
prescribed values on #{K}, the minimum of the sum is the sum
of the minima, once each local minimum is attained.}

\p{If #{U_i} is empty, the contribution of #{E_i} is already an
energy #{h(u,(-L_i)u)} on #{K}. If #{U_i} is nonempty and #{y}
supported on #{U_i} has #{h(y,(-L_i)y)=0}, every difference
along #{E_i} vanishes. Each vertex of #{U_i} is joined to a
vertex of #{K} by a path in #{E_i}, and #{y} vanishes on
#{K}, so #{y=0}. The compression #{\iota_{U_i}^{\dagger}(-L_i)\iota_{U_i}} is
therefore positive definite. The square completion recorded
in \ref{fdip-00DH} gives the unique minimum of the
#{L_i}-energy on that compression. The completion adds no
connectedness hypothesis and no invertibility of #{L_w}:
positive-definiteness here is the path condition just proved.
Distinct families may lie in distinct components.}

\p{Assemble the prescribed values on #{K}, the unique local
minimizer on each nonempty #{U_i}, and an arbitrary function
on #{Z}. The energy of this extension equals the sum of the
local minima and does not depend on the values on #{Z}. The
global minimum is therefore attained and equals that sum. It
is not unique when #{Z} is nonempty.}
}
